    pr_ref:  # 17f4
    description: "Parent: WI-razub-duluf-nobun-rulit-dapam-jipal-dafud-nahob (shipped mechanism lacks the \"meta-circuit-breaker\" the original design flagged).\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe agent-supervisor daemon (WI-rofuv) has ONE fork-bomb protection today: a soft 24h rate limit (default 8 spawns). That's rolling-window throttling, not pattern detection. It leaves three failure modes open:\n\n1. **Fast-fire tight loop.** 8 spawns in 5 minutes looks identical to 8 spawns spread across 23 hours. A freshly-respawned session that trips its own circuit breaker immediately (zero progress) burns through the day's budget in minutes, then the supervisor falls silent until midnight.\n2. **No chain-length memory.** The supervisor doesn't know \"respawn N was triggered because respawn N-1 died without doing anything useful\" — each session's `meta.json` is independent, so 30th-chained-failure-of-a-bootstrap-bug and 2nd-attempt-at-a-hard-problem look identical.\n3. **No auto-disable on persistent failure.** After 24h the oldest rate-limit entry drops off and the loop can start over. The supervisor has no kill switch for \"this keeps not working; stop trying.\"\n\nThe WI-razub design doc called this out as explicit **open question #2** (\"Anti-fork-bomb / intelligent breaker\"). The \"Roads not taken\" list dropped chain-length tracking in the interest of shipping, but the general concern was not resolved. The user raised it again on 2026-04-18 in direct discussion: \"Do we have mechanisms to handle this kind of failure mode?\" — the honest answer was \"the 24h soft cap is all we've got.\"\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd a proper meta-circuit-breaker to `scripts/agent-supervisor` with four pieces. Each piece alone is useful; the combination is the \"proper fix.\"\n\n### 1. Short-window fast-fire detection\n\nIn addition to the existing rolling-24h cap, add a short-window check. Proposal: **more than 3 spawns in a rolling 10 minutes** → the supervisor enters cooldown (default 30 minutes, configurable) during which it logs to `respawn_log.log` and skips every spawn. On cooldown exit, the short-window counter resets.\n\nThis catches the fast-fire tight loop within 15 minutes instead of 24 hours.\n\n### 2. Chain-length tracking in meta.json\n\nWhen the supervisor replaces a session, the new session's `meta.json` records `replaces: <old-session-id>` and `chain_length: <prior_chain_length + 1>`. The initial spawn (no predecessor) has `chain_length: 1`.\n\nThis gives the supervisor the memory it needs for the remaining three protections.\n\n### 3. Productive-failure detection + exponential backoff\n\nA session is \"productively failed\" if, at replacement time, its pane-byte delta from spawn-to-kill was below a small threshold (proposal: 512 bytes). That means the CLI barely rendered anything before getting stuck.\n\nWhen the supervisor decides to replace and the replaced session was productively-failed:\n- Record the failure count on the chain.\n- Sleep (instead of immediately spawning) for an exponentially-backed-off interval: 60s, 120s, 240s, 480s, …, capped at 1800s (30 min).\n- After the sleep, re-evaluate intent + attached clients before proceeding.\n\nProductive-success replacement (pane scrolled meaningfully before dying) resets the chain's failure count.\n\n### 4. Consecutive-failure kill switch\n\nAfter **5 consecutive productive-failures on the same chain**, the supervisor writes `supervisor.auto-paused` into its state directory and stops spawning entirely until the operator clears it (`rm` the file, or a new `agent-supervisor resume` subcommand). Also logs a prominent message to `respawn_log.log` with the chain tail.\n\nThis is the mechanism that says \"if my attempts to respawn keep failing, stop trying and ask for help.\"\n\n## Not in scope (deferred)\n\n- Auto-reporting / alerting the operator via non-file channels (email, Slack, desktop notification). The state file + log are enough for operators who run `agent-supervisor status`.\n- Cross-project chain tracking. Each project's supervisor has its own state directory; we don't correlate chains across workstations or repos.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Short-window detection trips at 4 spawns in 10 minutes.\n- Chain-length tracking increments correctly across a 3-replace sequence.\n- Productive-failure threshold: <= 512 bytes delta → failure; > 512 bytes → success.\n- Exponential backoff sleep durations: 60, 120, 240, 480, 960, 1800, 1800, …\n- Kill switch fires at the 5th consecutive productive-failure.\n- Kill switch does NOT fire when a successful session interrupts the chain.\n- `supervisor.auto-paused` file blocks future spawns until cleared.\n- Attached-client check still takes precedence during cooldown / backoff.\n- Decision matrix: `autonomous_intent=OFF` short-circuits before the meta-breaker logic runs (no wasted work).\n\n## Operator UX\n\n- `agent-supervisor status` surfaces: chain-length per session, consecutive-failure count, whether cooldown or auto-pause is active, time remaining on any backoff.\n- `agent-supervisor resume` clears `supervisor.auto-paused` and resets the chain counters. (New subcommand — small addition to the argparse tree.)\n- `docs/agent-supervisor.md` operator guide picks up the new `status` fields, the `resume` subcommand, and the fault patterns the meta-breaker guards against.\n\n## Governance\n\nTouches `scripts/agent-supervisor` (non-governance per the AGENTS.md list) and `docs/agent-supervisor.md`. Adds config knobs but the defaults are safe; no existing user behavior changes unless a fork-bomb actually occurs. Does NOT touch `.agent/hooks/**` or `AGENTS.md` (except a small pointer update from the existing Vendor Parity section if helpful) so no human approval is required beyond the scope of this ticket itself."  # 17f4
    fields: {}  # 17f4
